#: ../../electronic/exchange_correlation.rst:195
msgid ""
"この表では密度が高いほど交換によるエネルギー低下が大きい。結晶の平衡体積は、 "
"核間反発、電子の運動エネルギー、相関などを含めた全エネルギーの極小で決まる。 交換部分の密度依存は圧縮で動く項の一つである。"
msgstr ""
"The table shows that exchange lowers the energy more at higher densities."
" The equilibrium volume of a crystal is determined by the minimum of the "
"total energy, which includes internuclear repulsion, electron kinetic "
"energy, and correlation, among other terms. Exchange is one contribution "
"that changes with density under compression."

#: ../../electronic/exchange_correlation.rst:202
msgid "解釈と限界"
msgstr "Interpretation and Limitations"

#: ../../electronic/exchange_correlation.rst:204
msgid ""
"**近似の種類。** 一様電子ガスの表ではスピンの占有が等しく、交換だけを計算した。 "
"磁性がある系ではスピンごとの密度が交換に効く。実用のLDAやGGAでは相関も加え、 その近似を通じて計算結果が変わる。"
msgstr ""
"**Types of approximation.** The table for the uniform electron gas "
"assumes equal spin occupations and includes only exchange. In magnetic "
"systems, the density for each spin affects exchange. Practical LDA and "
"GGA functionals also include correlation, and the approximation used for "
"it affects the results."

#: ../../electronic/exchange_correlation.rst:207
msgid ""
"**汎関数の差と数値誤差。** 汎関数を比べる計算では、同じ格子と原子位置で 相対エネルギーを求めると、緩和で生じる差を切り分けられる。基底や\\"
" :ref:`k点<kpoint_sampling>` の誤差がその相対エネルギー差に近い場合は、汎関数を変えた効果を見分けにくい。"
msgstr ""
"**Differences between functionals and numerical errors.** To compare "
"functionals, calculate relative energies at the same lattice and atomic "
"positions to separate the effect of the functional from the differences "
"introduced by relaxation. If errors from the basis or \\ :ref:`k-points "
"<kpoint_sampling>` are comparable to the relative energy differences, the"
" effect of changing the functional is hard to distinguish."

#: ../../electronic/exchange_correlation.rst:210
msgid ""
"**構造と有限温度。** 小さな格子定数のずれでも、ひずみと結びついた相の エネルギー差には大きく効く場合がある。0 "
"Kの計算で近い格子定数を与えた 汎関数でも、有限温度の相境界を比べるには振動や熱膨張の寄与を考える。"
msgstr ""
"**Structure and finite temperature.** Even small deviations in lattice "
"constants can strongly affect energy differences between phases that are "
"coupled to strain. Even for a functional that gives lattice constants "
"close to experiment in a 0 K calculation, account for vibrational and "
"thermal-expansion contributions when comparing phase boundaries at finite"
" temperature."

